---
// Reader: a public-service owner considering an AI assistant as one optional
// citizen channel for a narrowly configured BReg service.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import DocsHandoff from '../../components/DocsHandoff.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Citizen access through an AI assistant | Registry Stack';
const pageDescription =
  'Help a signed-in person prepare a registry correction in chat, then review and submit it on the institution’s site.';
const mcpDocsHref = 'https://docs.registrystack.org/configure/breg-mcp/';
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <SiteHeader current="ai-citizen-access" />

  <main>
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="citizen-access-title">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI for citizen access</p>
          <h1 id="citizen-access-title">Help people prepare a request in chat.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            A compatible assistant can help a signed-in person read permitted details and prepare
            a correction. The person reviews and submits the draft on a separate page run for the
            institution.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href={mcpDocsHref}>Read the citizen assistant guide</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/ai/">Explore AI for public services</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">An experimental integration available for evaluation with a configured Base Registry Engine service.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="correction-example-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Fictional example</p>
          <h2 id="correction-example-title">“I moved. Can I update my address?”</h2>
          <p>
            Alex notices that the contact address in a register is out of date. The institution
            has approved a compatible assistant as one way to start a correction.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ol class="citizen-steps" aria-label="Fictional address correction through an assistant and institution review page">
          <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Alex signs in</h3>
              <p>Alex signs in through the approved assistant. The register uses that sign-in to identify Alex’s own record.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>The assistant prepares a draft</h3>
              <p>It reads the details the register permits and prepares a draft correction with Alex.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Alex opens the institution page</h3>
              <p>The assistant returns a review link. Alex signs in again on a separate page, compares the draft with the current record, and chooses whether to submit it.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>The register handles the submitted request</h3>
              <p>Base Registry Engine checks access and follows the institution’s rules for reviewing and applying the change. Alex can ask the assistant for the request’s status.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="authority-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading center">
          <p class="eyebrow">Institutional authority</p>
          <h2 id="authority-title">Configure what the assistant may see and prepare.</h2>
          <p>
            The institution chooses the service, identity provider, access profile, permitted
            fields, and task authority. The implementation connects and tests those parts before
            anyone uses the channel.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Approve the assistant and sign-in</h3>
            <p>Connect the institution’s sign-in service and agree how the assistant will handle the information it receives.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Define the allowed task</h3>
            <p>Specify which details the assistant can see and which fields it can include in a draft. The register checks that permission each time.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Separate preparation from submission</h3>
            <p>The institution’s review page uses a separate sign-in for Alex to review and submit the draft.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">An optional channel</p>
          <h2 id="scope-title">Start with one task your institution can support.</h2>
          <p>
            The integration uses Model Context Protocol (MCP) to connect an approved assistant to
            a configured registry service. The institution can keep its portal or another supported
            route available to people who prefer it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The service can run without an AI model. Add an assistant when you have agreed what it
            may do, how people will review the draft and who will operate the integration.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout" aria-labelledby="implementation-title">
          <h3 id="implementation-title">What your technical team connects</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A compatible assistant and approved client registration</li>
            <li>An identity provider that supports delegated access</li>
            <li>An external task authority that issues grants for each draft, including follow-up reads and edits, and reports whether those grants are still valid</li>
            <li>Separate gateway and review services with distinct credentials, run over a secure connection</li>
            <li>Testing for the exact records, fields, and correction action</li>
          </ul>
          <p><a href={mcpDocsHref}>Review the deployment conditions in Registry Docs</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="section-inner related-pages" aria-label="Related citizen access and architecture pages">
        <a class="inline-cta" href="/architecture/headless/">See the headless architecture <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        <a class="inline-cta" href="/digital-public-infrastructure/">Place the service within a digital public infrastructure programme <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <DocsHandoff
      eyebrow="Choose the next step"
      heading="Check what you need to offer the assistant channel."
      body="Start with the citizen task, the permitted details, and the point where the institution requires review."
      primaryLabel="Read the technical guide"
      primaryHref={mcpDocsHref}
      emphasis="docs"
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .citizen-steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .citizen-steps li {
    align-items: start;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(18px, 4vw, 40px);
    grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 34px) 0;
  }

  .citizen-steps li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
  }

  .step-number {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    font: 700 var(--type-base)/1.4 var(--registry-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .citizen-steps h3 {
    font-size: var(--type-2xl);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .citizen-steps p {
    font-size: var(--type-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .editorial-callout ul {
    line-height: 1.65;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .editorial-callout li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .related-pages {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px 32px;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .citizen-steps li {
      gap: 8px;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
